From b6b7a02fe2b47f9a2143daaec676a9687f626b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steffen Persvold <spersvold@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 11:37:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] drm/tiny: add ocfb DRM/KMS driver for the OpenCores
 VGA/LCD core

Add a DRM/KMS driver for the OpenCores VGA/LCD 2.0 core (ocfb) and
register-compatible derivatives, with optional support for a line-pitch
register, hardware scan doubling and a runtime-programmable pixel-clock
PLL. The hardware is a single-plane scanout engine, so it uses
drm_simple_display_pipe + GEM-DMA with fbdev emulation for the console.
It advertises a fixed list of CEA-861/VESA-DMT modes (the output has no
DDC/EDID) with correct sync polarity, reprograms the pixel-clock PLL on
mode set (M/N/C solver, max-pixclk-hz ceiling in mode_valid), and selects
register byte order from the generic "big-endian" DT property. Bound via
the "opencores,ocfb" compatible.

Make it mutually exclusive with the fbdev driver in Kconfig
(FB_OPENCORES depends on !DRM_OCFB), mirroring FB_SIMPLE/DRM_SIMPLEDRM.

The register definitions are derived from the OpenCores VGA/LCD core and
its fbdev driver (drivers/video/fbdev/ocfb.c) by Stefan Kristiansson.

Signed-off-by: Steffen Persvold <spersvold@gmail.com>
